{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Avraham was old, etc.</b> The explanation is that since he perceived himself to be old, and also saw that HaShem had magnified His goodness toward him with every blessing, he was concerned that the servant who rules over everything and sees abundant possessions — while the man who is master of all has grown old — would devise schemes to marry off his daughter to Yitzchak, for it would find favor in his eyes. Therefore he said to him <b>Place now your hand</b> etc.; he cleverly sought to have him swear an oath in a general manner concerning the Canaanite, so that his ears would hear the matter, for the sound would reach him and nullify his intent — for he [the Canaanite] is cursed, whereas Yitzchak is blessed, according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 59)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:56.222721697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}